{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1192"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge film-media/film","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/film-media__film.g2.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",606],["-","adopted,"],["+","adopted"],["=",1],["+","– which is why Fritz Lang is regarded as the inventor of the countdown – "],["=",178],["+","Lang left Germany in 1933, worked briefly in France and from 1934 in the United States, where he made more than twenty films, among them „Fury“ (1936) and „The Big Heat“ (1953). That double career is honoured on both sides of the Atlantic: Fritz Lang has a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame in Los Angeles and another on Berlin's Boulevard der Stars, opened in 2010 on Potsdamer Platz.\n\n"],["=",123]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",598],["-","übernahmen,"],["+","übernahmen"],["=",1],["+","– weshalb Fritz Lang als Erfinder des Countdowns gilt – "],["=",176],["+","Lang verließ Deutschland 1933, arbeitete kurz in Frankreich und ab 1934 in den Vereinigten Staaten, wo er mehr als zwanzig Filme drehte, darunter „Blinde Wut“ (1936) und „Heißes Eisen“ (1953). Diese doppelte Karriere wird auf beiden Seiten des Atlantiks gewürdigt: Fritz Lang hat einen Stern auf dem Hollywood Walk of Fame in Los Angeles und einen weiteren auf dem 2010 am Potsdamer Platz eröffneten Berliner Boulevard der Stars.\n\n"],["=",115]]}]},
